== CASE ==
AWPTCM-T44275  (207) Authentication&Security_WebAuthentication - Proxy Server for Web Authentication
ck.db (read at triage, queue lines 112-129): Status Draft; objective, precondition and steps NOT authored
(one empty step). Run from its title, per the triage plan: an unauthenticated client whose browser uses an
HTTP proxy (absolute-URI request to 8.8.8.8:8080) must get the DUT's login page once
`auth-web-server intercept-port 8080` is set, and NOT without it (control).
References: AAA and Port Authentication Feature Overview and Configuration Guide C613-22088-00 rev P p.52
("If you have an HTTP proxy server listening on TCP port 8080, you must configure ... auth-web-server
intercept-port 8080"); Technical Tips and Tricks AW+ rev D p.65 ("Web Auth proxy": with a browser proxy,
"the network on which the proxy server is located on must be added as a 'No Proxy' network").

Tools: tools/tb tool tb5 wa1528 httpq <url> --proxy 8.8.8.8:8080 (the --proxy option was ADDED to tools/httpq.py
for this case: urllib Request.set_proxy, request line `GET http://www.example.com/ HTTP/1.1` sent to the proxy;
checked on the dev host against a listener, it printed exactly that line). Captures:
tools/tb sudotool tb5 wa1528 arpleg --tag <t> --out /tmp/wa1528/t75 --iface eth6 --sniff-only
--filter 'tcp port 8080 or icmp' --wait 35|40 (started in the background, tcpdump gated with tools/tb ps).
